{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Equalise self-employed Maternity Allowance with Statutory Maternity Pay\r\n",
        "additional_details": "Self-employment does not give entitlement to Statutory Maternity Pay. Eligible self-employed mothers instead receive Maternity Allowance, which does not include the same earnings-related period as SMP. We believe mothers should receive equivalent maternity support regardless of employment status, and that Maternity Allowance should keep pace with future improvements to SMP, so that self-employed mothers are not left behind.",
        "background": "Reform the Maternity Allowance for self-employed mothers so they receive maternity support equivalent to Statutory Maternity Pay, including the same earnings-related periods and ensuring the Maternity Allowance receives the same increases or improvements that the SMP receives in the future.",
